ogle.com/open?id=1jHRh-eTe16RmYxb7V7VGivTU-9J6Hcy7\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=1jH...VGivTU-9J6Hcy7</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T08:26:19-07:00","id":1245495,"title":"","content":"Has anybody compiled lists or suggestions of &quot;combos&quot; to make, being Charms that harmonize well together?<br /> <br /> We got started working through DB chargen at my home table, but of course the shopping is as momentous as any Exalted game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:04:22-07:00","id":1245510,"title":"","content":"The guide is very much let down by a lack of granularity - bad/okay/good/very good is just not nearly as expressive as the D&amp;D CharOp boards-style bad/situational/average/good/very good split. <br /> <br /> Also, the rating of some picks is uhh... questionable at best. When Charms that have been sent back for a second pass for being borderline useless (Sky-Calming Draw, Flame-Borne Interception) are rated as good picks, I find myself futilely trying to unravel the logic behind the decision in bafflement (and failing, because - another cardinal sin in guide writing - the writer's reasoning is not made apparent, just their conclusion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:35:10-07:00","id":1245522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245495#post1245495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anybody compiled lists or suggestions of &quot;combos&quot; to make, being Charms that harmonize well together?<br /> <br /> We got started working through DB chargen at my home table, but of course the shopping is as momentous as any Exalted game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Essence do you want builds for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:45:07-07:00","id":1245527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245522#post1245522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Essence do you want builds for?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment, 2, as idea seeds for working through DB chargen. <br /> <br /> For comparison, when we did Solars chargen a while ago, it took us a couple of passes to get everybody together with a good selection of interlocking Charms. We decided together that we wanted to encourage some generalization, so everybody pretty much kept to 5 +- 2 combat Charms and had at least the ability to participate in combat, social scenes, and investigation/lore/sorcery/brainy scenes. <br /> <br /> That, above, isn't a requirement for builds, of course. Just explaining the idea of having a savant or diplomat who isn't made of jello in a fight, in a Circle with a warrior who is neither one-dimensional nor distorts the enemy stats too high. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:49:49-07:00","id":1245530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245510#post1245510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the rating of some picks is uhh... questionable at best. When Charms that have been sent back for a second pass for being borderline useless (Sky-Calming Draw, Flame-Borne Interception) are rated as good picks, I find myself futilely trying to unravel the logic behind the decision in bafflement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, SCD isn\u2019t that bad. If you\u2019re doing battle in a 1,000 year storm it\u2019s 4 motes to ignore a -5 penalty, and in a relatively heavy rain storm, sandstorm, or on a blustery wind swept plain its 4 motes to negate a -3 penalty. It\u2019s situational for sure but in those situations it\u2019s solid. The requirement to aim isn\u2019t even really that bad since so many of the other archery charms want you to aim you\u2019ll probably be doing it already.<br /> <br /> The part about extending range is basically completely useless. It\u2019s only applicable to Elemental Bolt Attack if I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:58:31-07:00","id":1245537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245527#post1245527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the moment, 2, as idea seeds for working through DB chargen. <br /> <br /> For comparison, when we did Solars chargen a while ago, it took us a couple of passes to get everybody together with a good selection of interlocking Charms. We decided together that we wanted to encourage some generalization, so everybody pretty much kept to 5 +- 2 combat Charms and had at least the ability to participate in combat, social scenes, and investigation/lore/sorcery/brainy scenes. <br /> <br /> That, above, isn't a requirement for builds, of course. Just explaining the idea of having a savant or diplomat who isn't made of jello in a fight, in a Circle with a warrior who is neither one-dimensional nor distorts the enemy stats too high. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that\u2019s easy to do with DBs, I\u2019ll make a thread and post some builds tonight. Do you want just like a skeleton build, or just advice on what charms/abilities work well together, or like full builds with all the merits and everything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:03:49-07:00","id":1245541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245537#post1245537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that\u2019s easy to do with DBs, I\u2019ll make a thread and post some builds tonight. Do you want just like a skeleton build, or just advice on what charms/abilities work well together, or like full builds with all the merits and everything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that comes to mind would be excellent idea seed material! <br /> <br /> Full builds would be great, especially if they come with some notes about how the build pulls together.<br /> <br /> Skeletons or groupings of charms would also be great, because they can be pretty easy to reuse. <br /> <br /> <br /> TYVM!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:12:29-07:00","id":1245543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245530#post1245530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, SCD isn\u2019t that bad. If you\u2019re doing battle in a 1,000 year storm it\u2019s 4 motes to ignore a -5 penalty, and in a relatively heavy rain storm, sandstorm, or on a blustery wind swept plain its 4 motes to negate a -3 penalty. It\u2019s situational for sure but in those situations it\u2019s solid.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First off, when a <i>literal demon storm out of hell with winds strong enough to force flying creatures out of the sky</i> only applies a -3, I'm strongly questioning how often a -5 is going to happen over the course of the average campaign.<br /> <br /> Second, yes - in a situation where you would take a -3, you can effectively use it to get +3 non-charm dice for 4m. It's a slightly worse motes-to-dice rate than the excellency, but those dice are non-charm, so it's fair. But that's all it is - fair. Not great. Not amazing.<br /> <br /> So what you have is a Charm that, if you fulfill a(n admittedly rather easily met) specific condition, negates a specific kind of penalty at worse-than-excellency rates of mote expenditure - meaning it's situational and <i>even in its niche</i>, not that great. In D&amp;D guide terms, it merits a purple rating (worse than average, but not outright bad). The problem is, the guide rates it as good, by which it presumably means &quot;better than average&quot;. That's two steps higher than it deserves. On a five step scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T10:42:15-07:00","id":1245550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245543#post1245543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First off, when a <i>literal demon storm out of hell with winds strong enough to force flying creatures out of the sky</i> only applies a -3, I'm strongly questioning how often a -5 is going to happen over the course of the average campaign.<br /> <br /> Second, yes - in a situation where you would take a -3, you can effectively use it to get +3 non-charm dice for 4m. It's a slightly worse motes-to-dice rate than the excellency, but those dice are non-charm, so it's fair. But that's all it is - fair. Not great. Not amazing.<br /> <br /> So what you have is a Charm that, if you fulfill a(n admittedly rather easily met) specific condition, negates a specific kind of penalty at worse-than-excellency rates of mote expenditure - meaning it's situational and <i>even in its niche</i>, not that great. In D&amp;D guide terms, it merits a purple rating (worse than average, but not outright bad). The problem is, the guide rates it as good, by which it presumably means &quot;better than average&quot;. That's two steps higher than it deserves. On a five step scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I don\u2019t necessarily agree with the guide, but the corebook example for a -3 penalty is perilous terrain or fog + high wind. Definitely not Adorjan the Silent Wind. If Adorjan in the book provides that kind of penalty it\u2019s probably some stacking magic thing, or just for balance reasons.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also an essence 1 archery 2 DB charm and is therefore a hair\u2019s breadth away from the absolute weakest class of charm in the game, and should be rated as such. You don\u2019t compare Meteor Swarm to Magic Missile. It\u2019s around FBI in tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T12:03:34-07:00","id":1245586,"title":"","content":"The guide is flawed because it tells you the ratings but it doesn't tell you why the charms are rated that way or the metrics for the ratings. I disagree that sifu's kindly quill is bad because it only applies bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T18:18:02-07:00","id":1245702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245541#post1245541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything that comes to mind would be excellent idea seed material!<br /> <br /> Full builds would be great, especially if they come with some notes about how the build pulls together.<br /> <br /> Skeletons or groupings of charms would also be great, because they can be pretty easy to reuse.<br /> <br /> <br /> TYVM!</div> </div> </div> </div>So... &quot;Tonight&quot; was ambitious, apparently I had too much stuff to do. I've got all the outlines ready I just need to get the specs down, it should be tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T19:47:01-07:00","id":1245727,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's the lack of explanations... but it kinda feels like these guides are also suffering from, well, Dragonblooded being the lowest power Exalted. I haven't looked at everything, but the sheer volume of Green and Orange when I look things over makes me feel like the guide was constantly thinking, &quot;But the Solar Charm set does X better, so lets knock it down a rating.&quot; It just feels like a lot of Charms would got up if there was a stronger eye to, &quot;is this good for a Terrestrial level character?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T02:29:27-07:00","id":1245806,"title":"","content":"Boughs of Burning Autumn seems very..Ehh. to me, in light of other options. 2m and 3i per shot is a bit much compared to Cloud of Ebon Devils, or the first evocations of Sirrush and Sekhem - it seems like, for people devoted to using flame weapons, reloading them quickly is fairly common.<br /> <br /> The advantage of Boughs of Burning Autumn is that it can be used to make multiple attacks, but that means you're adding a 2m and 3i surcharge to every shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T05:16:52-07:00","id":1245831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amayad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1244248-darkuwa-s-definitive-100-correct-db-charm-ratings-charm-buying-guide?p=1245806#post1245806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boughs of Burning Autumn seems very..Ehh. to me, in light of other options. 2m and 3i per shot is a bit much compared to Cloud of Ebon Devils, or the first evocations of Sirrush and Sekhem - it seems like, for people devoted to using flame weapons, reloading them quickly is fairly common.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's actually 2m 1i, but it still compares unfavorably to Cloud of Ebon Devils. It's Perilous, which shuts it down in Initiative Crash, and has a dead Charm as its prerequisite (it explicitly says it only works on &quot;a firewand or similar flame weapon&quot; - why am I forced to pick up a Charm that explicitly <i>can't help me</i> if I want to use a firewand? Either Harvest of the Hunter needs to be changed so it can create ammunition for flame weapons, or it shouldn't be a prerequisite here). Its supposed advantage is that it can a/ help you reload between multi-attacks (which is not an issue if you go for Righteous Devil instead), and b/ allows you to just reflexively reload, without the awkward aim requirement (but since Righteous Devil Form allows you to reflexively aim, this is only actually an advantage if you're really bad at Presence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:15:49-07:00","id":1245909,"title":"","content":"Based on feedback future guides will have comments for the reasoning behind ratings. I will also be going back and adding them to the old guides. Do people prefer the ones sorted by essence or by ability? Cause I'm only going to do it to one set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:34:06-07:00","id":1245917,"title":"","content":"Preferred to sort by Ability, and without descriptions. We can look up the Charms by name, so the document should just describe why the Charm deserves its rating, ideally with suggestions for how they could be improved or how overpowered Charms could be nerfed or cut into two good Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:08:27-07:00","id":1245939,"title":"","content":"Removing the descriptions would defeat the purpose for me. I do these because rewriting the charms in my own woulds helps me to understand them and remember them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:17:54-07:00","id":1245942,"title":"","content":"I find it much easier to grok with the short descriptions, tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T10:23:11-07:00","id":1245947,"title":"","content":"I think I slightly preferred the by-Ability grouping, because if (for instance) I'm figuring out how to improve my Thrown, I'd be opening up several docs to see all the options.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T18:46:04-07:00","id":1246500,"title":"","content":"Core book artifacts reviewed. Now with comments on ratings. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1f_dG9i34lYA6SN8Z0U7uYcKCnI8bzGEBvYYl3JpXMgY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T18:31:13-07:00","id":1246833,"title":"","content":"Arms artifacts are reviewed, now with comments <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Gxr_3fIfIxDs8Om0HVbVqCFxzTd7FTao\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Gx...bVqCFxzTd7FTao</a>","signature":"","edited":{"user